flint 0.7.0: builds Flint projects

Usage:
  flint <command> [options]

Commands:
  init      start a new project
  build     build the project's executable
  run       build the project and run it
  test      run the project's `test` blocks
  check     report compile errors without building
  fetch     download the project's dependencies
  clean     remove the project's build output
  help      show this overview, or a command's help
  version   print flint's version

Options:
  --release            the 'release' profile: optimized
  --profile=<name>     a profile of flint.toml; debug (the default) and release always exist
  -v, --verbose        show the commands that are run (the C compiler, flintc)
  --color=<when>       colored output: auto (default), always or never
  -h, --help           show this help

A project is a directory with a flint.toml: its name, dependencies, C sources and build
profiles. flint reads it and calls the compiler, flintc; for one file, use flintc itself.
'flint help <command>' has the details and examples.
